\pard\sb100\sa100\cf0\lang1033\line\cf2\b ArcTan2\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the arctangent angle and quadrant of a given number. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b ArcTan2\b0 (const Y: Extended, const X: Extended): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
ArcTan2 calculates ArcTan(Y/X), and returns an angle in the correct quadrant. The values of X and Y must be between -2^64 and 2^64. \par
In addition, the value of X can\rquote t be 0. The return value will fall in the range from -Pi to Pi radians. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf0\lang1033\line\cf2\b ArcTanH\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the inverse hyperbolic tangent of a given number. \par
