\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b FutureValue\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the future value of an investment. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b FutureValue\b0 (const \b Rate\b0 : Extended, \b NPeriods\b0 : Integer, const \b Payment\b0 : Extended, const \b PresentValue\b0 : Extended, \b PaymentTime\b0 : TPaymentTime): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\par
\b0  FutureValue returns the future value of an investment of \b PresentValue\b0  where \b Payment\b0  is invested for \b NPeriods\b0  at the rate of \b Rate\b0  per period. The \b PaymentTime\b0  parameter indicates whether the investment is an ordinary annuity or an annuity due (enter \b 0\b0  if payments are at the end of each period, \b 1\b0  if they are at the beginning). \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\par
