\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b NetPresentValue\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the current value from an array of estimated cash flow values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b NetPresentValue\b0 (const \b Rate\b0 : Extended, const \b CashFlows\b0 : array of Double (\b 1,2,3...,\b0 ), \b PaymentTime\b0 : TPaymentTime): Extended\par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
NetPresentValue calculates the current value of an array of estimated cash flow values, discounted at the given interest rate of \b Rate\b0 . \b CashFlows\b0  is the array of estimated cash flow values. \b PaymentTime\b0  indicates whether the cash flows occur at the beginning or end of the period (enter \b 0\b0  if payments are at the end of each period, \b 1\b0  if they are at the beginning). NetPresentValue helps determine how much an investment is currently worth, based on expected earnings, although its accuracy depends on the accuracy of the cash flows in the array.\par
