function \b Norm\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Norm returns the Euclidean 'L-2' norm for the values in the Data array. The 'L-2' norm is the square root of the sum of squares. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b NumberOfPeriods\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of payment periods for an investment. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b NumberOfPeriods\b0 (const \b Rate\b0 : Extended, \b Payment\b0 : Extended, const \b PresentValue\b0 : Extended, const \b FutureValue\b0 : Extended, \b PaymentTime\b0 : TPaymentTime): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
NumberOfPeriods computes the number of payment periods required for an investment of \b PresentValue\b0  to reach a value of \b FutureValue\b0 , while making regular payments of \b Payment\b0  and accruing interest at the rate of \b Rate\b0  per compounding period. \b PaymentTime\b0  indicates whether the cash flows occur at the beginning or end of the period (enter \b 0\b0  if payments are at the end of each period, \b 1\b0  if they are at the beginning).  \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Payment \cf0\b0 Routine Calculates a fully amortized payment. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Payment\b0 (\b Rate\b0 : Extended, \b NPeriods\b0 : Integer, const \b PresentValue\b0 : Extended, const \b FutureValue\b0 : Extended,\b  PaymentTime\b0 : TPaymentTime): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Payment calculates the fully amortized payment of borrowing \b PresentValue\b0  at \b Rate\b0  percent per period over \b NPeriods\b0 . It assumes that interest is paid at the end of each period. \b FutureValue\b0  is the value that the investment will reach at some point. \b PaymentTime\b0  indicates whether the cash flows occur at the beginning or end of the period (enter \b 0\b0  if payments are at the end of each period, \b 1\b0  if they are at the beginning).\line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b PeriodPayment\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the principal amount from a full payment. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b PeriodPayment\b0 (const \b Rate\b0 : Extended, \b Period\b0 : Integer, \b NPeriods\b0 : Integer, const \b PresentValue\b0 : Extended, const \b FutureValue\b0 : Extended, \b PaymentTime\b0 : TPaymentTime): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
PeriodPayment gives the part of the payment that is principal. The InterestPayment function gives the part of the payment that is interest. The \b Rate\b0  parameter is the interest rate. \b Period\b0  is the number of periods into the loan for which the principal is desired, and \b NPeriods\b0  is the number of periods of the loan. \b FutureValue\b0  is the value the investment will reach at some point. \b PaymentTime\b0  indicates whether the cash flows occur at the beginning or end of the period (enter \b 0\b0  if payments are at the end of each period, \b 1\b0  if they are at the beginning).\line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b PopnStdDev\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the population standard deviation.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b PopnStdDev\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
PopnStdDev calculates the population standard deviation (the square root of the population variance) of all values in the Data array parameter. This function is used in some business and financial calculations. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b PopnVariance\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the population variance.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b PopnVariance\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
PopnVariance calculates the population variance of all values in the Data array parameter, using the n method (biased): TotalVariance / n. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Power\cf0\b0  Routine Raises Base to any power.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Power\b0 (const AValue: TComplex, const APower: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Power raises Base to any power. For fractional exponents or exponents greater than MaxInt, Base must be greater than 0. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b PresentValue\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the present value of an investment. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b PresentValue\b0 (const \b Rate\b0 : Extended, \b NPeriods\b0 : Integer, const \b Payment\b0 : Extended, const \b FutureValue\b0 : Extended, \b PaymentTime\b0 : TPaymentTime): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
PresentValue calculates the present value of an investment where \b Payment\b0  is received for \b NPeriods\b0  and is discounted at the rate of \b Rate\b0  per period. \b FutureValue\b0  is the value the investment may reach at some point. \b PaymentTime\b0  indicates whether the cash flows occur at the beginning or end of the period(enter \b 0\b0  if payments are at the end of each period, \b 1\b0  if they are at the beginning).\line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b RadToDeg\cf0\b0  Routine Converts radians to degrees. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b RadToDeg\b0 (const Radians: Extended): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Use RadToDeg to convert angles measured in radians to degrees, where degrees = radians(180/pi). \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Sec, Secant\cf0\b0  Routines Calculates the secant of an angle. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Sec\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call Sec to obtain the secant of X, where X is an angle in radians. The secant is calculated using the formula 1 / Cos(X). \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b SecH\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates the hyperbolic secant of an angle. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b SecH\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call SecH to obtain the hyperbolic secant of X, where X is an angle in Radians. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Sign\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates whether a numeric value is positive, negative, or zero. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Sign\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Use Sign to test the sign of a numeric value. Sign returns 0 if AValue is zero. 1 if AValue is greater than zero. -1 if AValue is less than zero. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Sin\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the sine of the angle in radians. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Sin\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
In Delphi code, the Sin function returns the sine of the argument. X is a real-type expression. Sin returns the sine of the angle X in radians. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b SinH\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the hyperbolic sine of an angle. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b SinH\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Sinh calculates the hyperbolic sine of X. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b SLNDepreciation\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the straight-line depreciation allowance of an asset. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b SLNDepreciation\b0 (const \b Cost\b0 : Extended, const \b Salvage\b0 : Extended, \b Life\b0 : Integer): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
SLNDepreciation calculates the straight-line depreciation allowance for an asset over one period of its life. The function divides the \b Cost\b0  minus the \b Salvage\b0  by the number of years of useful \b Life\b0  of the asset. \b Cost\b0  is the amount initially paid for the asset. \b Salvage\b0  is the value of the asset at the end of its useful life.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Skew\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates skew.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Skew\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended;\par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\par
\b0 Skew calculates the core factors of statistical analysis: skew. Data specifies the data to be analyzed. Skew reflects symmetry of distribution. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b StdDev\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the sample standard deviation for elements in an array. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b StdDev\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
StdDev calculates the sample standard deviation (the square root of the sample variance) of all values in the Data array parameter.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Sum\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the sum of the elements in an array. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b Sum\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Sum returns the sum of all the values in the Data array parameter. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b SumOfSquares\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the sum of the squared values from a data array. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b SumOfSquares\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
SumOfSquares returns the sum of the squares of the Data values: Data[0]^2 + Data[1]^2 + Data[2]^2... \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Sqr\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the square of a number. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b Sqr\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
In Delphi code, the Sqr function returns the square of the argument. X is a floating-point expression. The result, of the same type as X, is the square of X, or X*X.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Sqrt\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the square root of X. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Sqrt\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
X is a Delphi floating-point expression. The result is the square root of X. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b SYDDepreciation\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates depreciation for an asset. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b SYDDepreciation\b0 (const \b Cost\b0 : Extended, const \b Salvage\b0 : Extended, \b Life\b0 : Integer,\b  Period\b0 : Integer): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
SYDDepreciation (for "sum-of-years-digits depreciation") calculates depreciation amounts for an asset using an accelerated depreciation method. This allows for higher depreciation in the earlier years of an asset's life. \b Cost\b0  is the initial cost of the asset. \b Salvage\b0  is the value of the asset at the end of its life expectancy.\b  Life \b0 is the length of the asset's life expectancy. \b Period\b0  is the period for which to calculate the depreciation\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Tan\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the tangent of X. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Tan\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Tan returns the tangent of X. Tan(X) = Sin(X) / Cos(X). \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b TanH\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the hyperbolic tangent of X. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b TanH\b0 (const AValue: TComplex): TComplex; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Tanh calculates the hyperbolic tangent of X. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b TotalVariance\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the statistical variance from an array of values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b TotalVariance\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
TotalVariance returns the sum of the squares of the difference between each Data value and the mean of the data values. Total Variance: SUM(i=1,N)[(X(i) - Mean)**2] \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\cf0\par
\lang1033\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\b Variance\cf0\b0  Routine Calculates statistical sample variance from an array of data. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b Variance\b0 (const Data: array of Double (\b 1,2,3...\b0 )): Extended; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Variance calculates the sample variance of all values in the Data array parameter, using the n-1 method (unbiased). \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049\par
