\cf1\fs40 Date and Time Routines Category\b  \par
\b0\f1\fs20 =====================================================\par
\cf0\f0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b CompareDate\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates the relationship between the date portions of two TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b CompareDate\b0 (const A: TDateTime, const B: TDateTime): TValueRelationship; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\par
\b0 Call CompareDate to compare the two TDateTime values specified by A and B. CompareDate returns LessThanValue if A occurs on a day prior to the day specified by B. EqualsValue if A occurs on the same day as B, ignoring the time of day. GreaterThanValue if A occurs on a day that follows the day specified by B.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b CompareDateTime\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates the relationship between two TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b CompareDateTime\b0 (const A: TDateTime, const B: TDateTime): TValueRelationship; \par
\cf3\b Description\par
\cf0\b0 Call CompareDateTime to compare the two TDateTime values specified by A and B. CompareDateTime returns LessThanValue if A is earlier than B. EqualsValue if A is the same as B. GreaterThanValue if A is later than B. \par
Note: Note:CompareDateTime differs from a direct comparison of the corresponding double precision values in that two TDateTime values are considered the same if they have the same value down to the millisecond. It is possible to create two TDateTime values that differ numerically when viewed as doubles, but which represent the same year, month, day, hour, minute, second, and millisecond. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b CompareTime\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates the relationship between the time portions of two TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b CompareTime\b0 (const A: TDateTime, const B: TDateTime): TValueRelationship; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\par
\b0 Call CompareTime to compare the two TDateTime values specified by A and B. CompareTime returns LessThanValue if A occurs earlier in the day than B (even if A occurs on a later day than B). EqualsValue if A occurs at the same time of day as B, ignoring of the date portion of the two values. GreaterThanValue if A occurs later in the day than B (even if A occurs on an earlier day than B).\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DateOf\cf0\b0  Routine Strips the time portion from a TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DateOf\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call DateOf to convert a TDateTime value to a TDateTime value that includes only the date information (sets the time portion to 0, which means midnight).\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DayOf\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the day of the month represented by a TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b DayOf\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call DayOf to obtain the day of the month represented by a specified TDateTime value. DayOf returns a value between 1 and 31. \par
Note: Note:DayOf returns the same value as the DayOfTheMonth function. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DayOfTheMonth\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the day of the month represented by a TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b DayOfTheMonth\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call DayOfTheMonth to obtain the day of the month represented by a specified TDateTime value. DayOfTheMonth returns a value between 1 and 31. \par
Note: Note:DayOfTheMonth returns the same value as the DayOf function. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DayOfTheWeek\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the day of the week represented by a TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b DayOfTheWeek\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call DayOfTheWeek to obtain the day of the week represented by a specified TDateTime value. DayOfTheWeek returns a value between 1 and 7, where 1 indicates Monday and 7 indicates Sunday. \par
Note: Note:DayOfTheWeek is ISO 8601 compliant (where Monday is considered the first day of the week). To obtain the day of the week where Sunday is considered the first day of the week, use the DayOfWeek function instead. \par
Note: Tip:To make the return value more readable, use the Day of week constants. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DayOfTheYear\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of days between a specified TDateTime value and December 31 of the previous year. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DayOfTheYear\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call DayOfTheYear to obtain the ordinal position of a TDateTime value\rquote s day within its year. Thus, a TDateTime value that refers to January 1 generates a result of 1, dates on January 2 return 2, dates on February 1 return 32, and so on.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DaysBetween\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of whole days between two specified TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DaysBetween\b0 (const ANow: TDateTime, const AThen: TDateTime): Integer; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call DaysBetween to obtain the difference, in days, between two TDateTime values. DaysBetween counts only whole days. Thus, DaysBetween reports the difference between Dec 31, 1999 11:59 PM and Jan 1, 2000 11:58 PM as 0 because the difference is one minute short of an entire day. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DaysInAMonth\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of days in a specified month of a specified year. \b Namespace\b0  Borland.Vcl.DateUtils \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b DaysInAMonth\b0 (const AYear: Word, const AMonth: Word): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call DaysInAMonth to obtain the number of days in the specified month of the specified year. AYear is a year between 1 and 9999 (inclusive). AMonth is a month between 1 and 12 (inclusive). \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DaysInMonth\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of days in the month of a specified TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DaysInMonth\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call DaysInMonth to obtain the number of days in the month of the TDateTime value specified by AValue. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DaysInAYear\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of days in a specified year. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DaysInAYear\b0 (const AYear: Word): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call DaysInAYear to obtain the number of days in the year specified by AYear. AYear is a year between 1 and 9999 (inclusive).\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DaysInYear\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of days in the year of a specified TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DaysInYear\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call DaysInYear to obtain the number of days in the year of the TDateTime value specified by AValue. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b DaySpan\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of days (including fractional days) between two specified TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b DaySpan\b0 (const ANow: TDateTime, const AThen: TDateTime): Double; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\par
\b0  Call DaySpan to obtain the difference, in days, between two TDateTime values. Unlike the DaysBetween function, which only counts whole days, DaySpan reports incomplete days as a fraction of an entire day. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b HourOfTheDay\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the hour of the day represented by a TDateTime value. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b HourOfTheDay\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call HourOfTheDay to obtain the hour of the day represented by a specified TDateTime value. HourOf returns a value between 0 and 23. \par
Note: Note:HourOfTheDay returns the same value as the HourOf function. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b HourOfTheMonth\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of hours between a specified TDateTime value and 12:00 AM of the first day of the month. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b HourOfTheMonth\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call HourOfTheMonth to obtain the number of complete hours between AValue and 12:00 AM on the first day of the month that includes AValue. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b HourOfTheWeek\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of hours between a specified TDateTime value and 12:00 AM of the first day of the week.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b HourOfTheWeek\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call HourOfTheWeek to obtain the number of complete hours between AValue and 12:00 AM on Monday of the week that includes AValue. \par
Note: Note:HourOfTheWeek defines the week of AValue according to the ISO 8601 standard. That is, the week starts on Monday and ends on Sunday. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b HourOfTheYear\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of hours between a specified TDateTime value and 12:00 AM of the first day of the year. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b HourOfTheYear\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Word; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call HourOfTheYear to obtain the number of complete hours between AValue and 12:00 AM on Jan 1 of the year that includes AValue. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b HoursBetween\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of whole hours between two specified TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b HoursBetween\b0 (const ANow: TDateTime, const AThen: TDateTime): Int64; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call HoursBetween to obtain the difference, in hours, between two TDateTime values. HoursBetween counts only entire hours. Thus, HoursBetween reports the difference between 9:00 AM and 9:59:59 AM as 0 because the difference is one second short of an entire hour. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b HourSpan\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of Hours (including fractional Hours) between two specified TDateTime values. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b HourSpan\b0 (const ANow: TDateTime, const AThen: TDateTime): Double; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
Call HourSpan to obtain the difference, in hours, between two TDateTime values. Unlike the HoursBetween function, which only counts entire hours, HourSpan reports incomplete hours as a fraction of an entire hour.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncDay \cf0\b0 Routine Returns a date shifted by a specified number of days. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b IncDay\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfDays: Integer): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IncDay returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfDays days. ANumberOfDays can be negative, to return a date N days previous. The time of day specified by the AValue parameter is copied to the result. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncHour\cf0\b0  Routine Returns a date/time value shifted by a specified number of hours.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b IncHour\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfHours: Int64): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IncHour returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfHours hours. ANumberOfHours can be negative, to return a date and time N hours prior to AValue. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncMilliSecond\cf0\b0  Routine Returns a date/time value shifted by a specified number of milliseconds. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b IncMilliSecond\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfMilliSeconds: Int64): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\b0  \cf0\par
IncMilliSecond returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfMilliSeconds milliseconds. ANumberOfMilliSeconds can be negative, to return a date and time N milliseconds prior to AValue. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncMinute\cf0\b0  Routine Returns a date/time value shifted by a specified number of minutes. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b IncMinute\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfMinutes: Int64): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IncMinute returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfMinutes minutes. ANumberOfMinutes can be negative, to return a date and time N minutes prior to AValue.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncSecond\cf0\b0  Routine Returns a date/time value shifted by a specified number of seconds. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b IncSecond\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfSeconds: Int64): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IncSecond returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfSeconds seconds. ANumberOfSeconds can be negative, to return a date and time N seconds prior to AValue\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncWeek\cf0\b0  Routine Returns a date shifted by a specified number of weeks.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b IncWeek\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfWeeks: Integer): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IncWeek returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfWeeks weeks. ANumberOfWeeks can be negative, to return a date N weeks previous. The time of day specified by the AValue parameter is copied to the result.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IncYear\cf0\b0  Routine Returns a date shifted by a specified number of years.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b IncYear\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ANumberOfYears: Integer): TDateTime; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IncYear returns the value of the AValue parameter, incremented by ANumberOfYears years. ANumberOfYears can be negative, to return a date N years previous. The time of day specified by the AValue parameter is copied to the result.\par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IsInLeapYear\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates whether a specified TDateTime value occurs in a leap year.\par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b IsInLeapYear\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Boolean; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
Call IsInLeapYear to determine whether the year of the date specified by AValue occurs in a leap year. \par
\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IsPM\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates whether the time portion of a specified TDateTime value occurs after noon. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\cf0\b0  \par
function \b IsPM\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime): Boolean; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IsPM returns true if the time portion of AValue occurs on or after 12:00 noon and before 12:00 midnight. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b IsSameDay\cf0\b0  Routine Indicates whether a specified TDateTime value occurs on a the same day as a criterion date. \par
\cf3\b Syntax\b0  \cf0\par
function \b IsSameDay\b0 (const AValue: TDateTime, const ABasis: TDateTime): Boolean; \par
\cf3\b Description\cf0\b0  \par
IsSameDay returns true if AValue occurs on the same day as ABasis. The time portions of AValue and ABasis can differ. IsSameDay returns false if the date portions of AValue and ABasis differ. \line\pard\cf1\lang1049 =====================================================\par
\cf0\par
\pard\sb100\sa100\cf2\lang1033\b MilliSecondOfTheDay\cf0\b0  Routine Returns the number of milliseconds between a specified TDateTime value and the beginning of the same day. \par
